A university has introduced a new course registration system where students can enroll in courses.
Each course has a difficulty level (points required) and belongs to a specific department (category).
Students have a certain academic standing (point level) and are pre-approved for certain departments based on their major/minor.
A student can successfully register for a course only if:

They are pre-approved for that department (the department is in their approved list).
Their point level is greater than or equal to the course's required points.

Students may attempt to register for the same course multiple times (or different students may try), but once registered, the spot is taken (marked as completed).
Input
text4
Alice Johnson,7,ComputerScience Mathematics
